# No takebacks

**Nothing rerolls or cancels a landed die. Anywhere. Ever.** Not an item, not a
joker, not a skill, not a spell, not a difficulty setting, not a boss mercy
rule (LAWS.md #dice).

Dice land and stand. The only play after the roll is the **skill window** — a
limited-use skill spent *after seeing the result* — or the choice of action
(`THROW` / `GATHER` / `BRACE`), or flee. All of those are decisions made with
the outcome visible. None of them erases it.

That is the entire agency layer, and it only means anything if the die is
final. A reroll turns every roll into a resource check and every tense moment
into arithmetic.

`retrigger`, `extra-throw`, and anything re-entering scoring are **banned in
v0** (F5). Not deferred — banned, until an amendment card argues otherwise and
carries the termination proof with it.

